{"seconds": 52.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Good! After Nxf2+ from Kh1 line, Black also wins the pawn. But the Kh3 line looks cleaner with the winning Nxe3+ and Nxc4 combo. The main variation is:\n\n**1...Bxh2+ 2.Kxh2 Ng4+ 3.Kh3 Nxe3+ 4.Qg4 Nxc4**\n\nThis wins a full piece (bishop for White gets captured after the knight takes it).\n\nNow let me write the coaching note:\n\n**Best move:** Bxh2+\n\n**Main line:** Bxh2+ Kxh2 Ng4+ Kh3 Nxe3+ Qg4 Nxc4\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Coaching Note (for club player):**\n\nYour knight on f6 is perfectly placed to exploit the exposed white king. After Bxh2+ (sacrificing the bishop for an attack), White must capture. Then Ng4+ creates a deadly fork\u2014checking the king while the knight eyes critical squares like e3. After Kh3, Nxe3+ keeps the initiative, winning the undefended bishop on c4. This pattern\u2014sacrificing material to unleash a piece for a powerful fork\u2014wins material back by force.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bxh2+\", \"line\": [\"Bxh2+\", \"Kxh2\", \"Ng4+\", \"Kh3\", \"Nxe3+\", \"Qg4\", \"Nxc4\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1rbq1k1r/p4ppp/2pb1n2/2p5/2B1N3/4PQ2/PP1P1PPP/R1B1R1K1 b - - 1 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "1rbq1k1r/p4ppp/2pb1n2/2p5/2B1N3/4PQ2/PP1P1PPP/R1B1R1K1 b - - 1 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "1rbq1k1r/p4ppp/2pb1n2/2p5/2B1N3/4PQ2/PP1P1PPP/R1B1R1K1 b - - 1 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1rbq1k1r/p4ppp/2pb1n2/2p5/2B1N3/4PQ2/PP1P1PPP/R1B1R1K1 b - - 1 12", "move": "Bxh2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1rbq1k1r/p4ppp/2p2n2/2p5/2B1N3/4PQ2/PP1P1PPb/R1B1R1K1 w - - 0 13", "move": "Kxh2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1rbq1k1r/p4ppp/2p2n2/2p5/2B1N3/4PQ2/PP1P1PPb/R1B1R1K1 w - - 0 13", "move": "Kh1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r